# Case-insensitive default autoescape extensions

## Goal

Make Flask's default Jinja autoescape selection recognize supported template
extensions regardless of filename case, so templates such as `invoice.HTML`
and `diagram.SvG` receive the same default autoescaping as their lowercase
counterparts.

## Confirmed Facts

- `Flask.select_jinja_autoescape` in `src/flask/sansio/app.py` is the default
  policy used when Jinja's `autoescape` option is not explicitly configured.
- The current policy returns `True` for `None` and otherwise uses a
  case-sensitive suffix check for `.html`, `.htm`, `.xml`, `.xhtml`, and
  `.svg`.

## Requirements

- Treat the supported default autoescape extensions case-insensitively.
- Preserve `True` for a `None` filename.
- Preserve `False` for filenames whose extension is not supported.
- Keep the change restricted to the existing default behavior and its tests.

## Acceptance Criteria

- [ ] Each supported extension enables autoescaping for lowercase, uppercase,
      and mixed-case filename spellings.
- [ ] `None` still enables autoescaping.
- [ ] Unsupported or extensionless filenames still do not enable autoescaping.
- [ ] The public test suite passes.

## Out of Scope

- Changing custom Jinja `autoescape` configuration behavior.
- Adding new supported extensions or changing the supported-extension list.

## Open Questions

- None. The requested behavior and repository evidence fully determine this
  lightweight change.
